From: jbuck2005 <59450931+jbuck2005@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: r8125: don't report work from the "other" vector at budget 0

netpoll (netconsole) calls every NAPI poll of the device with a budget of 0
to clean Tx only, and warns once if a poll returns non-zero:

  WARNING: net/core/netpoll.c:157 ... exceeded budget in poll

The Rx and Tx polls return 0 at budget 0, but rtl8125_poll_msix_other()
always completed NAPI and returned 1. With a
budget of 0 return 0 straight away; that vector has no Tx work.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8125/r8125_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8125/r8125_n.c
@@ -17234,6 +17234,14 @@
         (void)(dev);
         (void)(work_to_do);
 
+        /*
+         * netpoll (netconsole) polls with a budget of 0 to clean Tx only.
+         * This vector has no Tx work; it must neither complete NAPI nor
+         * report work it was not given budget for.
+         */
+        if (!budget)
+                return 0;
+
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4,10,0)
         RTL_NETIF_RX_COMPLETE(dev, napi, work_to_do);
 #else
